      "writtenOn": "2022-11-16T20:30:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can\u0027t Data be defined (with appropriate type) based on the test result implementation? It seems unnecessary to have this here as a generic type.\n\nFor example, can\u0027t we have Data defined as a field of BazelTestResult?",
      "revId": "c1850d1feca29511d60d921f0807d7bf9f3999dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f3e5ebb6_6e1ab2ca",
        "filename": "android/fixture.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 689,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-17T11:17:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately not without a large amount of restructuring. BazelTestResult depends on BazelTargets which is defined in the bp2build package. The bp2build package depends on android package. In order for TestResult to depend on BazelTestResult there would need to be a dependency from android back to bp2build which would create a dependency cycle between packages which is not supported in go.\n\nThis was the best I could do to allow us to tunnel information from the FixtureTestRunner to the tests.\n\nIf Go had generics we might be able to do better ...",
      "parentUuid": "75a48a81_f030e9ea",
      "revId": "c1850d1feca29511d60d921f0807d7bf9f3999dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "67720612_85b8755c",
        "filename": "android/fixture.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 689,
      "author": {
        "id": 1605027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-30T23:56:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not suggesting that TestResult should depend on BazelTestResult. I think that this Data field should not exist in this struct at all. Nothing in this package depends on the Data field (it just initializes it to an empty map, but otherwise is not referenced).\n\nWe could thus have the BazelTestResult be:\n\n```\ntype BazelTestResult struct {\n\t*android.TestResult\n\tData map[string]BazelTargets\n}\n```\n\nand we need not change the rest of the code. Is that not correct?",
      "parentUuid": "f3e5ebb6_6e1ab2ca",
      "revId": "c1850d1feca29511d60d921f0807d7bf9f3999dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31a943a3_b86de94a",
        "filename": "android/fixture.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 689,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-12-01T14:30:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately, not. It\u0027s difficult to follow in Gerrit but the `BazelTargets` are only returned by `GenerateBazelTargets` which is called in the bazel implementation of `PostParseProcessor(*TestResult)`. The targets need to be tunneled out to the test that called `result :\u003d ...RunTest()`. The `TestResult.Data` field is used for that purpose.\n\nI think that I made this more confusing than necessary with the way that I wrapped the `*TestResult` in a `BazelTestResult` in order to set the fields and then just discarded it. That was a holdover from my attempts to try a better approach before I ended up with the `Data` idea.\n\nI can\u0027t return `*BazelTestResult` instead of `*TestResult` because even though `*BazelTestResult` embeds a `*TestResult` it is not a `*TestResult`. In Java that would work but then in Java we could use generics which would be even better.\n\nNow, if instead of `*TestResult` `RunTest()` returned a `TestResult` interface then it would work, the Bazel tests would just need to downcast to `*BazelTestResult`. I could add a `RunTestWithCustomResult() CustomTestResult` to do that so instead of doing this:\n```\nresult :\u003d preparer.RunTest(t)\nbazelResult :\u003d BazelTestResult{result}\n```\n\nYou would have to do this:\n```\nbazelResult :\u003d preparer.RunTestWithCustomResult(r).(*BazelTestResult)\n```\n\nWhich is slightly better but not that big a saving. It would make it easier to access the individual fields, and to add new data to tunnel through.\n\nWould you like me to do that instead?",
      "parentUuid": "67720612_85b8755c",
      "revId": "c1850d1feca29511d60d921f0807d7bf9f3999dc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
